stateDiagram-v2
    classDef neutral fill:#1e293b,stroke:#475569,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#f8fafc
    classDef gate fill:#312e81,stroke:#6366f1,stroke-width:2px,color:#e0e7ff
    classDef confirmed fill:#450a0a,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#fecaca
    classDef nonliquet fill:#451a03,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#fef3c7
    classDef refuted fill:#064e3b,stroke:#059669,stroke-width:1.5px,color:#a7f3d0
    classDef deliverable fill:#172554,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px,color:#bfdbfe

    [*] --> ScopeTriage
    ScopeTriage: <b>Step 0: Scope & Triage</b><br/><i>Pick What Matters Most First:</i><br/>Inventory all entry doors and rank by danger<br/>(Money movement > State updates > Reads)
    
    ScopeTriage --> PickCandidate: Candidate Pool
    PickCandidate: <b>Candidate Selection</b><br/><i>Pick:</i> Grab highest-risk feature or scanner alert

    state AuditProcedure {
        [*] --> Facts
        Facts: <b>Step 1: Observed Facts</b><br/><i>Trace the Pipeline:</i><br/>Map path from user click to database save<br/>Record exact files, lines, and database tables
        
        Facts --> Boundaries
        Boundaries: <b>Step 2: Hard Boundaries</b><br/><i>Inspect the Guardrails:</i><br/>Is it all-or-nothing in a single transaction?<br/>Can concurrent clicks break balance?
        
        Boundaries --> Reconstruct
        Reconstruct: <b>Step 3: Competing Paths</b><br/><i>Imagine Worst-Case Reality:</i><br/>Stress-test duplicate clicks, network drops,<br/>crashes mid-checkout, and out-of-order retries
        
        Reconstruct --> Degradation
        Degradation: <b>Step 4: Degradation Check</b><br/><i>Unmask Hidden Failures:</i><br/>Find errors swept under the rug<br/>(swallowed exceptions, un-awaited tasks, fallbacks)
        
        Degradation --> Trust
        Trust: <b>Step 5: Trust Dynamics</b><br/><i>Assume Caller Is Hostile:</i><br/>Does code blindly trust IDs, prices, or headers?<br/>Can users edit prices or peek at other accounts?
        
        Trust --> FailurePoint
        FailurePoint: <b>Step 6: Failure Mapping</b><br/><i>Find the Exact Crime Scene:</i><br/>Pinpoint the line of code where logic breaks<br/>(e.g., line 42 double-spend via missing lock)
    }

    PickCandidate --> AuditProcedure: Begin Investigation
    AuditProcedure --> EvidenceGate: Decision Gate
    
    EvidenceGate: <b>Step 7: The Verdict Gate</b><br/><i>Refuse to Guess:</i><br/>Sort findings into 3 strict proof categories

    EvidenceGate --> ConfirmedProof: Provable Breach
    EvidenceGate --> NonLiquet: Indeterminate Path
    EvidenceGate --> RuledOut: Defense Discovered

    ConfirmedProof: <b>CONFIRMED (Real Bug)</b><br/>Reachable flaw - zero blocking defenses exist
    NonLiquet: <b>NON LIQUET (Need More Data)</b><br/>Code is tangled or hidden by external services
    RuledOut: <b>REFUTED (False Alarm)</b><br/>Looks risky, but underlying DB constraint keeps it safe

    ConfirmedProof --> FindingArtifact: Generate Reproducer
    NonLiquet --> TelemetrySpec: Specify Logs
    RuledOut --> CoverageNote: Mark Protected

    FindingArtifact: <b>Proof Dossier</b><br/>Write runnable test exploiting the bug<br/>Emit formal [FINDING-XXX] report
    TelemetrySpec: <b>Telemetry Spec</b><br/>Request exact log lines or metrics needed<br/>Emit formal [NON-LIQUET-XXX] spec
    CoverageNote: <b>Coverage Record</b><br/>Document verified defense so team knows it is safe

    FindingArtifact --> LoopCheck
    TelemetrySpec --> LoopCheck
    CoverageNote --> LoopCheck

    LoopCheck: <b>Scope Inspection Gate</b><br/><i>Check Backlog:</i> Unchecked entry points left?

    LoopCheck --> PickCandidate: More Features in Queue
    LoopCheck --> ReportDeliverable: All Code Audited
    
    ReportDeliverable: <b>Final Forensic Deliverable</b><br/>Hand engineering the complete dossier:<br/>What broke, proof scripts, and proven safe zones
    ReportDeliverable --> [*]

    class ScopeTriage,PickCandidate,LoopCheck neutral
    class EvidenceGate gate
    class ConfirmedProof,FindingArtifact confirmed
    class NonLiquet,TelemetrySpec nonliquet
    class RuledOut,CoverageNote refuted
    class ReportDeliverable deliverable
